# Rename Related Files Together

When the user asks to rename a file, rename all directly related sibling files that share the same base name.

## Rule

- Start from the exact file the user asked to rename.
- If sibling files in the same directory share the same base name, rename them too.
- Update all imports/usages that reference any renamed file.
- Keep suffixes/extensions intact while changing only the shared base name segment.
- Do not rename files with different base names unless the user explicitly asks.

## Common Related Patterns

- `foo.ts` -> `bar.ts`
- `foo.test.ts` -> `bar.test.ts`
- `foo.test.tsx` -> `bar.test.tsx`
- `foo.spec.ts` -> `bar.spec.ts`
- `foo.helper.ts` -> `bar.helper.ts`
- `foo.style.ts` -> `bar.style.ts`
- `foo.types.ts` -> `bar.types.ts`

## Example

- If renaming `use-session-tab-bar-visibility.ts` to `use-session-screeen-tab-bar-visibility.ts`, also rename `use-session-tab-bar-visibility.test.tsx` to `use-session-screeen-tab-bar-visibility.test.tsx` and update imports.
